<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- ============================================================================
         CSX v1 BASELINE, part 2 of 2: the SBSR response-leg spine.

         THIS IS THE VERSION 1 BASELINE. Every DCRE database is dropped and recreated
         at the v1 cutover, so this changelog only ever runs against an EMPTY schema.
         That is why the usual re-run guards are absent, and their absence is
         deliberate rather than an oversight:

           - no IF-NOT-EXISTS on the create. It guarded a create that might meet an
             already-migrated database. On an empty schema this CREATE is the first
             and only one, so the clause could not fire, and a clause that cannot
             fire would silently skip the create if the table were ever present for a
             reason nobody intended, turning a loud failure into a missing table.
           - no onFail="MARK_RAN" preconditions. The pre-v1 set carried two: one on
             the emission_id add-column and one on the response_file widening. Both
             tested for the retrofit having already happened. There is no retrofit
             here, because the column and the width are declared once, in this
             createTable.

         Pure typed tags, no raw-SQL body: the previous form hid its DDL from static
         analysis (the cleanout audit's first extractor could not see relations
         created inside a raw-SQL body) and pinned the file to one dialect.

         response_file is VARCHAR(512), which is the FINAL width and not the
         VARCHAR(128) the pre-v1 create declared. SCRUM-58 (spec 1.4): a reply name
         registers in agt_ops against file_arrival.physical_filename(512), so a 129+
         character name used to crash this reader's insert after the arrival had
         already been recorded. A v1 baseline has nothing to widen, so the separate
         modifyDataType changeset and its CockroachDB USING-clause workaround are
         gone with it: the column is simply born at the width it has to hold.

         emission_id correlates each reply verdict to the CRW emission batch that
         carried its e2e (crw_emission.outbound_msg_id, SCRUM-55). It is a plain UUID
         with NO foreign key: crw_emission is owned by CRW, and a cross-service FK on
         the shared dcre_col database would make one service's availability another's
         dependency. NULL when CRW's registry does not know the OrgnlMsgId, which is
         the fail-open ingest / fail-closed correlation contract.

         UNIQUE (response_file, e2e) is the replay guard: it is the full business
         identity of a verdict, and the ON CONFLICT target that makes re-ingesting a
         reply file a no-op rather than a duplicate.
         ============================================================================ -->

    <changeSet id="csx-v1-sbsr-resp" author="dcre">
        <createTable tableName="sbsr_resp">
            <column name="id" type="UUID" defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="response_file" type="VARCHAR(512)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="orgnl_msg_id" type="VARCHAR(35)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="emission_id" type="UUID"/>
            <column name="e2e" type="VARCHAR(35)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="status" type="VARCHAR(8)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="reason" type="VARCHAR(8)"/>
            <column name="version" type="BIGINT" defaultValueNumeric="0">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="created_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="updated_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </createTable>
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="sbsr_resp" columnNames="response_file, e2e"
                             constraintName="uq_sbsr_resp_file_e2e"/>
        <createIndex tableName="sbsr_resp" indexName="ix_sbsr_emission">
            <column name="emission_id"/>
        </createIndex>
        <rollback>
            <dropTable tableName="sbsr_resp"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
